I'd suggest to wait a little.  Sometimes, antique weapon shops 
provide you with great weapons, and anyway your god will eventually 
grant you some weapons, so weapons are maybe not the best choice 
to wish for.  Everything else can wait a little, Barbarians are not 
so desperately needing more stuff at the beginning.[1]  I would at the 
very least wait until after Sokoban to decide about more wishes.  
(I would even consider wishing for nothing before Soko, since then 
one can make the decision about SDSM/GDSM depending on wether one 
got "oR or or not.  But it's too late for that now, I guess ;-).)
If you really want to go on, Gauntlets of Power are very useful, 
as are Speed Boots (faster than the speed intrinsic).  In case you 
want to wish for artifatcs, have a look at Dylan's artifact spoiler 
to decide which one suits you best.  If you have a spare wish, you 
may consider to wish for a blessed fixed +3 T-Shirt, but this may 
also be found deeper in the dungeons.  Plus, you should be careful 
about sinks and unid-ed potions (make the unicorn test first) while 
wearing a T-Shirt, even in GDSM.

Best,
Jakob

[1] You _can_ face YAAD/YASD while going on, and may be angry about 
    not having used the whishes first.  But, on the other hand, this 
